          "distinct": false,
          "id": "056f8650d02c81e6589f2836dd58ea7796fd8e28",
          "message": "ci(bench): scope the perf gate under change-based selection + nightly full backstop (sq-mel85) [SONNET-4.6] (#1555)\n\n* ci(bench): scope the perf gate under change-based selection + nightly full backstop (sq-mel85) [SONNET-4.6]\n\nPhase 2b of the change-based test-selection design (research/change-based-\ntest-selection.md §5.2 — perf-gate = phase 2), deferred from sq-fmx4u.6. Mirrors\nthe fuzz/wasm conventions PR #1510 shipped.\n\nWHAT\n\n- bench.yml now calls the reusable ci-select.yml pre-job (unconditional `select`\n  job) and guards the `bench` job on its benchmarked-crate closure:\n    mode != 'selected'\n    || contains(affected, '\"sparq-engine\"'/'\"sparq-cli\"'/'\"sparq-bench\"'/'\"sparq-wasm\"')\n  Single source of truth: `_LANE_SEEDS[\"bench\"]` in scripts/ci_select.py, mirrored\n  in ci/path-ownership.toml [lanes], pinned by test_ci_select_wiring.py.\n- Nightly `schedule` full-run backstop added (05:29 UTC, offset from ci.yml 03:17\n  + fuzz.yml 04:23). A schedule event carries no PR diff => ci_select.py returns\n  mode=full => the bench lane runs the whole suite + hard gate (design §6.1).\n\nSEED SOUNDNESS\n\nSeeds are the closure of the HARD-GATED (merge-blocking) perf metrics: store/dict/\nparse byte metrics come from sparq-core (reached via the release binaries the job\nbuilds — sparq-cli + sparq-bench — which depend on core), and wasm_bundle_bytes\ncomes from sparq-wasm. sparq-wasm is a DIRECT seed on purpose: that floor is\nenforced ONLY in bench.yml and a wasm-only diff does not flow up into\nengine/cli/bench, so omitting it would silently drop the bundle gate for a\nwasm-only PR — the unsound skip §2 forbids. Trend-only latency metrics\n(geo/text/rsp/hdt/vectors/solid/nlq/zk) are advisory, not gates, so they are not\nseeds; every metric is still measured on the always-full push-to-main + nightly\nbackstop. Measured selectivity: bench skips 30/49 single-crate PRs, runs 19.\n\nMAIN CONTINUITY (criterion d — fail-closed)\n\npush-to-main + schedule are not pull_request/merge_group events, so ci_select.py\nreturns mode=full and the leading `mode != 'selected'` disjunct RUNS the full\nsuite on every main commit. Selection can ONLY narrow on pull_request/merge_group.\nThe auto-ratchet floor + benchmark-data history + Pages-dashboard steps are\nre-scoped from `github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'` to\n`github.event_name != 'schedule' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'` so the new\nnightly backstop verifies the gate WITHOUT committing a floor or pushing a\nduplicate per-commit history point — push-to-main (and workflow_dispatch)\nbehaviour is unchanged.\n\nVERIFY\n\n- actionlint clean (bench.yml, ci-select.yml); YAML + TOML valid.\n- test_ci_select.py 58 pass, test_ci_select_wiring.py 31 pass,\n  test_path_ownership.py 21, test_ci_summary_gate.py 33 — gate aggregator intact.\n- Hermetic dry-run (ci_select.py --changed-file --metadata-file): engine-touching\n  => RUNS, docs-only (research/**, SAFE) => SKIPS, wasm-only => RUNS (bundle floor),\n  isolated rsp-only => SKIPS; push/schedule => mode=full => RUNS FULL.\n\nNo crates/ source changed. SHA-pins untouched (reuses the in-repo ci-select.yml).\n\nCloses sq-mel85.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci/bench): correct false rationale in bench seed docs + pin metric-tier invariant (sq-mel85) [SONNET-4.6]\n\nThe shipped rationale described fts/vectors/geo mode:auto ratchets as\n\"trend-only/advisory\" and \"not merge-blocking\" — both false. They ARE\nmode:auto hard ratchets in bench/perf-baseline.json.  The SOUND invariant\nis: a hard-gated metric needs a bench seed only if ci-bench.sh measures\nit on the PR/merge_group tier; fts/vectors/geo are main-tier-only (GITHUB_REF\nguards at ci-bench.sh skip them on any non-main ref), so they need no seed.\n\nChanges (comment/doc only + one new invariant-pinning test):\n\n1. scripts/ci_select.py _LANE_SEEDS bench bullet: replace false \"trend-only/\n   advisory\" rationale with the true invariant (main-tier-only measurement ⇒\n   no seed needed; PR-tier hard gates ← store/dict/parse/wasm_bundle ← already\n   covered by sparq-core via release binaries + sparq-wasm direct seed).\n\n2. ci/path-ownership.toml [lanes] bench comment: same correction.\n\n3. scripts/tests/test_ci_select.py::test_cli_linked_crate_runs_bench_conservatively:\n   reword \"cannot move a HARD-GATED metric\" → \"cannot move a PR-tier-measured\n   hard-gated metric (geo_compliance_deficit is main-tier-only, where mode=full)\".\n\n4. scripts/tests/test_ci_select_wiring.py:\n   - TestPhase2LaneScoping::test_bench_main_history_and_ratchet_exclude_schedule:\n     add \"Clean bench-induced tracked churn before history switch (main only)\"\n     to the pinned schedule-exclusion step list (reviewer nit).\n   - New TestBenchMetricTierInvariant class: pins that every mode:auto metric in\n     bench/perf-baseline.json is either (a) inside a GITHUB_REF guard block in\n     ci-bench.sh (main-tier-only — verified by guard-range detection, no hardcoded\n     line numbers) or (b) PR-tier with a bench seed covering its source crate.\n     A future PR-tier promotion of fts/vectors can no longer silently drop a hard gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
